From: Zaviya-RM6 <exclaim_plethora227@simplelogin.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 07:22:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: pci: accept QCA6490 1.1 as WCN6855 hw2.1

The QCA6490 in SM8350 phones such as the REDMAGIC 6 reports SoC version
1.0x10. Its firmware (WLAN.HSP.1.1, the downstream amss.bin) is the one
WCN6855 2.1 uses, and ath11k runs it with the hw2.1 parameters.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pci.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pci.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pci.c
index 7114eca..1a02cbf 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pci.c
@@ -1031,6 +1031,16 @@ static int ath11k_pci_probe(struct pci_dev *pdev,
 		ath11k_pci_read_hw_version(ab, &soc_hw_version_major,
 					   &soc_hw_version_minor);
 		switch (soc_hw_version_major) {
+		case 1:
+			/*
+			 * QCA6490 1.1, as in SM8350 phones (REDMAGIC 6): the
+			 * downstream driver runs it with the same firmware
+			 * (WLAN.HSP.1.1, amss.bin) as WCN6855 2.1.
+			 */
+			if (soc_hw_version_minor != 0x10)
+				goto unsupported_wcn6855_soc;
+			ab->hw_rev = ATH11K_HW_WCN6855_HW21;
+			break;
 		case 2:
 			switch (soc_hw_version_minor) {
 			case 0x00:
-- 
